    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='D3 – Sales Over Time'>
      <style>
        <style-rule element='table'>
          <format attr='background-color' value='#000354' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='20536' id='5' type-v2='text' w='79852' x='9902' y='893'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>📈 </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Unispace' fontsize='14'>Sales soared, then stalled.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Cascadia Code' fontsize='12'>Global video game sales climbed for nearly three decades, hitting a peak between 2005 and 2009 during the rise of major consoles and blockbuster titles. But after 2010, the momentum shifted. Sales started falling, likely due to the industry’s pivot toward mobile, digital platforms, and streaming.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Unispace' fontsize='12'>Insight: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Cascadia Code' fontsize='12'>Understanding this timeline helps GameCo spot what worked, what changed, and what to prepare for in the next cycle of gaming demand.</run>
