              </zone>
              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='26451' id='10' type-v2='text' w='67047' x='14533' y='893'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>🕹️</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Unispace' fontsize='14'>Æ </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Unispace' fontsize='14'>GameCo isn’t alone, but it’s in competitive company.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Cascadia Code' fontsize='12'>Just five publishers dominate a massive slice of global sales. Nintendo leads by a wide margin, followed by EA and Activision. This isn’t just about numbers. It shows how big-name brands can control visibility, shelf space, and player loyalty.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Cascadia Code' fontsize='12'>Insight:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Cascadia Code' fontsize='12'> To grow its share, GameCo needs a strong IP strategy and smart partnerships, especially when stacked against giants.</run>
                </formatted-text>
